        "original_id": "90183a31-f437-5428-96c8-ff84602fd2c5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Idrissa Ouédraogo, Jerry Paris\n- Products: Yaaba, Police Academy 2: Their First Assignment\n- Places: Banfora, Upper Volta, Burkina Faso, Africa\n- Topics: Film directing, African cinema, The Dick Van Dyke Show, Police Academy series\n\nFacts:\n- Jerry Paris was born on July 25, 1925, and he was an American actor and director.\n- Idrissa Ouédraogo was born on 21 January 1954 in Banfora, Upper Volta.\n- Idrissa Ouédraogo was a film director from Burkina Faso who made films set in Africa.\n- Idrissa Ouédraogo often explored conflicts between rural and city life and between tradition and modernity in his films.\n- Yaaba is a 1989 Burkinabé drama film written, produced, and directed by Idrissa Ouédraogo.\n- Jerry Paris was best known for playing Jerry Helper, the dentist and next-door neighbor of Rob and Laura Petrie, on The Dick Van Dyke Show.\n- Police Academy 2: Their First Assignment was the first of six sequels in the Police Academy series.\n- Jerry Paris died on March 31, 1986.",
